lso unhealthy in staging.) We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55623, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019NypawVnui1nySjMUSxfbr", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_not_found", "safe_retry_with_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55623, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019NypawVnui1nySjMUSxfbr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59625, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy in every production region, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Check after rollback:** health checks are passing and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0 and the recovery. It also lists a follow-up: find the root cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again.\n\nThe test build of v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging before it went to production. It's worth finding out why it was released anyway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013QHGZ